<Layout title="About this prototype | Short Programs Prototype" description="Learn why this independent Astro website prototype was created and understand its limitations.">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">About this project</p><h1>An independent prototype for evaluation.</h1><p class="lede">This website explores how Astro could support clear, maintainable information for short-term inbound study programs at a Japanese university.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="container split align-start"><article class="prose"><h2>Purpose</h2><p>The prototype demonstrates a modern page system, reusable components and structured program content. It is intended for technical and design evaluation—not recruitment, admissions or publication.</p><h2>What is fictional</h2><p>All names, locations, dates, fees, deadlines, course descriptions and accommodation details were written as samples. No real student stories or university-confidential information are included.</p><h2>What it does not do</h2><p>There is no application process, account area, form submission, payment, analytics or tracking. Content should not be treated as academic, financial, immigration or travel advice.</p></article><aside class="notice-card"><p class="eyebrow">Please note</p><h2>Not an official website</h2><p>This is a prototype website created for evaluation purposes. It is not an official university website.</p><a class="text-link" href="/">Return home →</a></aside></div></section>
</Layout>
